Subject: [PATCH 4/4] QuickTTY managed launch, reader EOF and bounded terminal tail
Origin: QuickTTY local fix (not an upstream backport)
Base-Commit: 332b2aefc6e72d363aa93ab6ecfc86eeeeb5ed28 (after patches 0001-0003)

Add explicit managed-only helper launch and atomic reader completion state.
Read the current bounded terminal tail under the renderer lock with bounded
suffix storage. Preserve normal launch behavior and existing public C layouts.
New quicktty-prefixed exports are private to this embedding integration.
Ghostty MIT license applies. Runtime verification remains outstanding.

